window.__F=window.__F||{};window.__F["tr-07.html"]="<div class=\"ac-info\"><p class=\"ac-i-main\">الشرح الأصلي بالإنكليزية.</p><p class=\"ac-i-tip\"><b>متى تستعمله:</b> ابحث بالرمز أو بالاسم الإنكليزي. تأكد من نوع ناقل الحركة بسيارتك قبل ما تتبع دليل معيّن.</p><div class=\"ac-chips\"><span class=\"en-chip\">P = نقل الحركة: 10</span><span class=\"en-chip\">U = اتصال الشبكة: 9</span></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong>كيف تقرأ كود العطل</strong><small>الرقم بعد الشرطة يدل على نوع العطل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-legend\"><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-11</b><span>قصر على الأرضي</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-12</b><span>قصر على البطارية</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-13</b><span>دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-15</b><span>قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-16</b><span>الفولتية أقل من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-17</b><span>الفولتية أعلى من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-2A</b><span>مفتاح عالق Stuck</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-84 / 85</b><span>الإشارة أقل / أعلى من المدى</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-92</b><span>أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-00</b><span>عطل عام أو بدون نوع محدد</span></div></div><p class=\"bcm-note\">الحرف الأول: B = كهرباء الجسم · C = الهيكل والحساسات · P = نقل الحركة · U = اتصال الشبكة. نفّذ دائماً الفحص المسبق Pre-Diagnostic قبل خطوات أي كود.</p></div></details></div><input type=\"search\" class=\"ec-search acc-q\" placeholder=\"ابحث: كود العطل أو كلمة من الوصف\" aria-label=\"بحث\"><p class=\"bcm-note acc-cnt\">19 كود عطل. اضغط على الكود لترى شرحه.</p><div class=\"acc-list\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p0607-00 ecu internal performance esm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P0607-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ECU INTERNAL PERFORMANCE ESM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) performs various internal tests to verify proper controller operation. This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) indicates there is an issue with the ESM internal processor.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">When the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) is in it&#x27;s awake state.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) has detected an internal micro controller or memory failure.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">All ESM indicators and backlighting will be turned off. Gear selection will not be available.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</li><li>Always perform the Pre-Diagnostic Troubleshooting procedure before proceeding. Refer to PRE-</li><li>DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all ESM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Reconnect all ESM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Reconnect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read ESM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) in accordance with the Service information. Refer to MODULE, ELECTRONIC SHIFT (ESM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p0814-00 transmission range display circuit\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P0814-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TRANSMISSION RANGE DISPLAY CIRCUIT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) performs various internal tests to verify proper controller operation. This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) indicates that there is a problem with the Shifter indicator Light Emitting Diodes (LEDs).</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">ESM is awake on the CAN bus. Electronic Shift Module (ESM) Voltage between 6 and 16 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">A fault is detected if one of the following conditions is present for 500 milliseconds: Shifter indicator Light Emitting diode (LED) circuit failure. Shifter indicator over-temperature condition.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Shifter indicator will not illuminate. A Stored Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will be cleared after 100 ignition cycles if the failure does not reoccur.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) connector and all related in- line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the ESM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ELECTRONIC SHIFT (ESM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p0820-00 gear lever x-y position sensor circuit\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P0820-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">GEAR LEVER X-Y POSITION SENSOR CIRCUIT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) performs various internal tests to verify proper controller operation. This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) indicates that there is an internal error with the ESM.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. Electronic Shift Module (ESM) voltage between 6 and 16 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The ESM has detected an internal error with one or both of the internal position sensors.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The ESM will initiate the following Default Actions only if both position sensors are faulted: Shifter background Light Emitting Diodes (LEDs) will be disabled (off). Gear Selector indicator LEDs will blink. ESM will not send a gear selection signal to the Transmission Control Module (TCM). The ESM will send Signal Not Available (SNA) messages out on the Controller Area Network</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">(CAN) C bus and the CAN Dedicated Powertrain (DPT) bus. A stored DTC can only be cleared with the scan tool.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) connector and all related in- line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the ESM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ELECTRONIC SHIFT (ESM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p0930-00 btsi control circuit low\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P0930-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BTSI CONTROL CIRCUIT LOW</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) performs various internal tests to verify proper controller operation. This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) indicates that there is an internal error with the Brake Transmission Shift Interlock (BTSI) Solenoid that is located within the ESM assembly.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. Electronic Shift Module (ESM) voltage between 6 and 16 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">A fault is detected if one of the following conditions is present: With the Brake Transmission Shift Interlock (BTSI) Solenoid commanded on: The ESM detects a BTSI solenoid current draw above a calibrated value for 200ms. With the BTSI Solenoid commanded off: The ESM detects a BTSI solenoid current draw above a calibrated value for 200ms.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Shifter may be stuck in PARK or NEUTRAL (Mechanical override may be required to shift). Shifter unblock function may be disabled. (Shifter can be moved without applying the brake pedal.) A fault flag message is sent to the Transmission Control Module (TCM). A Stored Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will be cleared after 100 ignition cycles if the failure does not reoccur.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all ESM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Reconnect all ESM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Reconnect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read ESM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) in accordance with the Service information. Refer to MODULE, ELECTRONIC SHIFT (ESM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p0931-00 btsi control circuit high\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P0931-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BTSI CONTROL CIRCUIT HIGH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) performs various internal tests to verify proper controller operation. This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) indicates that there is an internal error with the Brake Transmission Shift Interlock (BTSI) Solenoid that is located within the Shifter assembly.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met: Ignition on. Electronic Shift Module (ESM) voltage between 6 and 16 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">With the Brake Transmission Shift Interlock (BTSI) Solenoid commanded on: The ESM detects a BTSI solenoid current draw below a calibrated value for 200ms.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Shifter may be stuck in PARK or NEUTRAL (Mechanical override may be required to shift). A fault flag message is sent to the Transmission Control Module (TCM). A Stored Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will be cleared after 100 ignition cycles if the failure does not reoccur.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all ESM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Reconnect all ESM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Reconnect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read ESM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) in accordance with the Service information. Refer to MODULE, ELECTRONIC SHIFT (ESM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1c86-14 prndl display-circuit short to ground or open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1C86-14</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PRNDL DISPLAY-CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND OR OPEN</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي أو دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) performs various internal tests to verify proper controller operation. This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) indicates that there is a problem with the Shifter backlighting Light Emitting Diodes (LEDs).</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. Electronic Shift Module (ESM) voltage between 6 and 16 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">A fault is detected if one of the following conditions is present for 25 seconds: Shifter backlighting Light Emitting Diode (LED) circuit failure. Shifter backlighting over-temperature condition.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Shifter backlighting will not illuminate. A Stored Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will be cleared after 100 ignition cycles if the failure does not</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">reoccur. ESM will continue to transmit the correct sensed gear selector position.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) connector and all related in- line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the ESM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ELECTRONIC SHIFT (ESM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1c8b-16 battery voltage - circuit voltage below threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1C8B-16</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY VOLTAGE - CIRCUIT VOLTAGE BELOW THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أقل من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) performs various internal tests to verify proper controller operation. This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) indicates that there is a problem with the battery supply voltage.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the ignition is on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electronic Shift Module (ESM) sensed battery voltage is below 6 volts for 15 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Shifter backlighting may not illuminate. Brake Transmission Shift Interlock (BTSI) may not function properly. Gear selector indicator Light Emitting Diodes (LEDs) may not function properly. Gear selector may not be able to shift gears. Controller Area Network (CAN) communication may be degraded. A Stored Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will be cleared after 100 ignition cycles if the failure does not reoccur.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CHARGING SYSTEM DTCS</li><li>ESM POWER AND GROUND CIRCUITS</li><li>ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR ENGINE CHARGING SYSTEM DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCs)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Powertrain Control Module (PCM) DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any Engine Charging System DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair Engine Charging System DTCs. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) POWER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ESM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the ESM battery power circuit at the ESM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the ESM power circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK GROUND CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the ESM ground circuit in the ESM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Reconnect all disconnected harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, clear ESM DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the Engine and raise the engine speed to 2, 000 rpm for 10 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read ESM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the ESM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ELECTRONIC SHIFT (ESM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1c8b-17 battery voltage - circuit voltage above threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1C8B-17</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY VOLTAGE - CIRCUIT VOLTAGE ABOVE THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أعلى من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) performs various internal tests to verify proper controller operation. This DTC indicates that there is a problem with the battery supply voltage</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the ignition is on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Electronic Shift Module (ESM) sensed battery voltage is above 16 volts for 15 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Shifter backlighting may not illuminate. Brake Transmission Shift Interlock (BTSI) may not function properly. Gear selector indicator Light Emitting Diodes (LEDs) may not function properly. Gear selector may not be able to shift gears. Controller Area Network (CAN) communication may be degraded. A Stored Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will be cleared after 100 ignition cycles if the failure does not reoccur.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CHARGING SYSTEM DTCS</li><li>ESM POWER AND GROUND CIRCUITS</li><li>ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR CHARGING SYSTEM DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTCs)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Powertrain Control Module (PCM) DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any Charging System DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair Charging System DTCs. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK IF VEHICLE WAS JUMP STARTED WITH 24-VOLT SYSTEM</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         Some Recreational Vehicles (RVs), Buses, and Semi Tractors use 24-volt systems.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Ask the customer if the vehicle was jump started by a vehicle with a 24-volt charging system.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Was the vehicle jump started by a vehicle with a 24-volt charging system?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">This is the cause of the DTC. Erase the DTC and return the vehicle to the customer.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK INDICATED ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) BATTERY VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the Engine and raise the engine speed to 2, 000 rpm.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, monitor the ESM Battery Voltage for 60 seconds.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the ESM Battery Voltage read above 16 volts at any time during the test?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>COMPARE ESM VOLTAGE TO BATTERY VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Raise the engine speed to 2, 000 rpm.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the ESM Battery Voltage.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the voltage at the Battery.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Compare the readings.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the measured voltage reading match the scan tool ESM Battery Voltage reading?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the Charging System for an over charging condition in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the ESM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ELECTRONIC SHIFT (ESM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1c8c-16 system voltage-circuit voltage below threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1C8C-16</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SYSTEM VOLTAGE-CIRCUIT VOLTAGE BELOW THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أقل من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) monitors the Controller Area Network (CAN) messages from the Body Control Module (BCM). If the BCM sends a system low voltage message, this Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the ignition is on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) has received a low voltage message from the Body Control Module (BCM) indicating that the system voltage is below 10.5 volts for more than 15 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">A Stored Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will be cleared after 100 ignition cycles if the failure does not reoccur.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) DTCs</li><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Electronic Shift Module (ESM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ESM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) DTCs</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, check for BCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are DTCs set in the BCM?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair BCM DTCs. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Body Control Module (BCM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the BCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, BODY CONTROL (BCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1c8c-17 system voltage-circuit voltage above threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1C8C-17</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SYSTEM VOLTAGE-CIRCUIT VOLTAGE ABOVE THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أعلى من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) monitors the Controller Area Network (CAN) messages from the Body Control Module (BCM). If the BCM sends a system high voltage message, this Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the ignition is on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) has received a high voltage message from the Body Control Module (BCM) indicating that the system voltage is above 16 volts for more than 15 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">A Stored Diagnostic trouble Code (DTC) will be cleared after 100 ignition cycles if the failure does not reoccur.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) DTCs</li><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Electronic Shift Module (ESM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ESM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) DTCs</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, check for BCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are DTCs set in the BCM?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair BCM DTCs. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Body Control Module (BCM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the BCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, BODY CONTROL (BCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0002-88 can c bus off performance-bus off\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0002-88</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CAN C BUS OFF PERFORMANCE-BUS OFF</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For a complete wiring diagram refer to appropriate SYSTEM WIRING DIAGRAMS article .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For an in-depth explanation of the CAN system operation, refer to the DESCRIPTION in Section 8E, COMMUNICATION.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on, off, run, or accessory. System voltage between 6 and 16 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) looses communication with other modules on the Controller Area Network (CAN) C bus.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If CAN Dedicated Powertrain (DPT) is still functioning: Shifter Light Emitting Diodes (LEDs) will be illuminated to full daytime brightness. ESM will communicate over CAN DPT bus. If both CAN C and CAN DPT are not functioning:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Brake Transmission Shift Interlock (BTSI) solenoid will be disabled. (Shifter may be locked in PARK or Neutral.) Gear selection will be disabled. Shifter indicator LEDs will be turned on. Shifter background illumination LEDs will be turned off. A Stored Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will be cleared after 100 ignition cycles if the failure does not reoccur.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CAN C CIRCUIT OPEN CIRCUIT</li><li>CAN C CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>CAN C CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>OTHER CAN C MODULE SHORTED INTERNALLY</li><li>ELECTRONIC SHIFT CONTROL MODULE (ESM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          If the scan tool will not communicate with CAN C, proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C .</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, run a Vehicle Scan Report and attached it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the Vehicle Scan Report, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>ATTEMPT TO LOCATE AN INTERMITTENT CIRCUIT FAULT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The scan tool LOSS OF COMM TEST will force the modules on the CAN C bus to continuously ping each other.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, initiate the LOSS OF COMM TEST.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A value above 0 under the NUMBER OF NO RESPONSES can help indicate the location of a circuit fault while wiggling the related CAN C bus circuits.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The scan tool lag time between pings is almost 1 full second. Keep this in mind while wiggling the wires and connectors.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>In a systematic manner, wiggle the applicable CAN C circuits at each related module, in-line connector, and Star Connector while monitoring the NUMBER OF NO RESPONSES on the scan tool.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the above test help locate the fault?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform repairs as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>PERFORM VISUAL INSPECTION OF CONNECTORS, TERMINALS AND WIRES</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all CAN C related modules harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Reconnect all CAN C related modules harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Reconnect all in-line harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Using the Vehicle Scan Report, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">The conditions that caused this DTC to set are no longer present. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0074-00 dedicated powertrain (dpt) can bus off\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0074-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DEDICATED POWERTRAIN (DPT) CAN BUS OFF</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) communicates with other controllers on the Controller Area Network (CAN) Dedicated Powertrain (DPT) bus. If the ESM looses communication with the other modules on the CAN DPT bus, a Loss of Communication or CAN bus Off Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on, off, run, or accessory.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">System voltage is between 6 and 16 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) looses communication with other modules on the Controller Area Network (CAN) Dedicated Powertrain (DPT) bus.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If CAN C is still functioning: ESM will continue to communicate over the CAN C bus. Customer will not notice any problems with vehicle. If both CAN DPT and CAN C are not functioning: Brake Transmission Shift Interlock (BTSI) solenoid will be disabled. (Shifter may be locked in PARK or Neutral.) Gear selection will be disabled. Shift indicator Light Emitting Diodes (LEDs) will be turned on. Shifter background illumination LEDs will be turned off. A Stored Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will be cleared after 100 ignition cycles if the failure does not reoccur.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CAN DPT CIRCUIT OPEN CIRCUIT</li><li>CAN DPT CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>CAN DPT CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>OTHER CAN DPT MODULE SHORTED OR OPEN INTERNALLY</li><li>ELECTRONIC SHIFT CONTROL MODULE (ESM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Electronic Shift Control (ESM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ESM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE CONTROLLER AREA NETWORK (CAN) DEDICATED POWERTRAIN (DPT) CIRCUIT VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ESM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (D441) CAN DPT (+) circuit at the ESM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (D440) CAN DPT (-) circuit at the ESM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage between 2.4 and 2.6 volts for each circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the ESM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ELECTRONIC SHIFT (ESM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK CAN DPT CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the TCM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D441) CAN DPT (+) circuit between the ESM harness connector and the TCM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D440) CAN DPT (-) circuit between the ESM harness connector and the TCM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms for each circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the affected CAN DPT circuit(s) for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK CAN DPT CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (D441) CAN DPT (+) circuit at the TCM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (D440) CAN DPT (-) circuit at the TCM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the either of the CAN DPT circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the affected CAN DPT circuit(s) for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK CAN DPT CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO ANOTHER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (D441) CAN DPT (+) circuit and all other circuits at the TCM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for continuity between the (D440) CAN DPT (-) circuit and all other circuits at the TCM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between either CAN DPT circuit and any other circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the affected CAN DPT circuit(s) for a short to another circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the ESM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ELECTRONIC SHIFT (ESM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0101-08 lost communication with tcm-bus signal / message failures\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0101-08</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH TCM-BUS SIGNAL / MESSAGE FAILURES</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع TCM-BUS SIGNAL / MESSAGE FAILURES</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) communicates with other controllers on the Controller Area Network (CAN) C bus and CAN Dedicated Powertrain (DPT) bus. The ESM expects to receive certain messages at certain time intervals from other controllers. If one message is missing, the ESM will not take any action. If more than one message is missing, the ESM will set a Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC).</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage message received over the Controller Area Network (CAN) is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. If system voltage over CAN is not available, Electronic Shift Module (ESM) sensed voltage is used and must be between 6.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN C Bus Off Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTCs) set. The ESM is programmed. The Transmission Control Module (TCM) is available on the CAN bus.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">An expected message from the TCM is not received for more than 300ms.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If CAN DPT is still functioning: ESM will continue to communicate over the CAN DPT bus. Customer will not notice any problems with the vehicle. If both CAN Dedicated Powertrain (DPT) and CAN C are not functioning: Brake Transmission Shift Interlock (BTSI) solenoid will be disabled. (Shifter may be locked in PARK or Neutral.) Gear selection will be disabled. Shift indicator Light Emitting Diodes (LEDs) will be blinking. Shifter background illumination LEDs will be turned off. The DTC will be Stored immediately once the ESM receives the message it was expecting.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INTERMITTENT CAN C CIRCUIT CONNECTIONS</li><li>MODULE SENDING THE CAN C MESSAGES</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Electronic Shift Module (ESM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ESM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK CONTROLLER AREA NETWORK (CAN) C CIRCUITS FOR INTERMITTENT CONDITIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Visually check the CAN C circuits and connectors for the following conditions: Intermittent open circuit Intermittent short to ground Intermittent short to other circuits Connector terminal corrosion Proper connector terminal tension</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Transmission Control Module (TCM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ELECTRONIC SHIFT (ESM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0140-00 lost communication with body control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0140-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH BODY CONTROL MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع BODY CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0155-00 lost communication with cluster-ccn\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0155-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH CLUSTER-CCN</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع CLUSTER-CCN</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0402-00 implausible data received from tcm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0402-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM TCM</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من TCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0422-00 implausible data received from body control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0422-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM BODY CONTROL MODULE</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من BODY CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For a complete wiring diagram, refer to appropriate SYSTEM WIRING DIAGRAMS article .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Sensor information and other calculated data that is processed by an Electronic Control Module (ECU) can be transmitted over the Controller Area Network (CAN). Some ECUs require information from other ECUs to check the validity of the information relative to that system. In some cases that information is used in the calculations relative to that ECU.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the transmitting ECU knows that the data is not valid, it will transmit a CAN message indicating that the information is not valid or not available. Often, this message is known as a Signal Not Available (SNA) message.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When a SNA message is transmitted, a Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will be set in the receiving ECU.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If a SNA message is received, this indicates that the transmitting ECU cannot transmit good data relative to the information that it was supposed to send. Typically, the transmitting ECU will also have a DTC set related to that information. Therefore, in most cases, this DTC is considered informational because the error is related to another ECU.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage message received over Controller Area Network (CAN) is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts If system voltage over CAN is not available, Electronic Shift Module (ESM) sensed voltage is used and must be between 6.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN C Bus Off Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. The ESM is programmed. The Body Control Module (BCM) is available on the CAN bus.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The BCM has transmitted a message indicating that the expected data is not valid.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Background lighting will default to maximum daytime intensity. The DTC will be Stored once the ESM receives valid data related to the information it was expecting. A Stored DTC will be cleared after 100 ignition cycles if the failure does not reoccur.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) DTCS ARE SET</li><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Electronic Shift Module (ESM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ESM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) FOR DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read BCM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any BCM DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair BCM DTCs. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Body Control Module (BCM) connector and all</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the BCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, BODY CONTROL (BCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u11c3-00 esm lost communication with tcm on d-pt can\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U11C3-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ESM LOST COMMUNICATION WITH TCM ON D-PT CAN</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Shift Module (ESM) communicates with other controllers on the Controller Area Network (CAN) Dedicated Powertrain (DPT) bus. If the ESM looses communication with the other modules on the CAN DPT bus, a Loss of Communication or CAN bus Off Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage message received over Controller Area Network (CAN) is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts If system voltage over CAN is not available, Electronic Shift Module (ESM) sensed voltage is used and must be between 6.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN C Bus Off Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. The ESM is programmed. The Transmission Control Module (TCM) is available on the CAN bus.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The ESM looses communication with the TCM on the CAN DPT bus for more than 300ms.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If CAN C is still functioning: ESM will continue to communicate over the CAN C bus. Customer will not notice any problems with vehicle. If both CAN Dedicated powertrain (DPT) and CAN C are not functioning: Brake Transmission Shift Interlock (BTSI) solenoid will be disabled. (Shifter may be locked in PARK or Neutral.) Gear selection will be disabled. Shift indicator Light Emitting Diodes (LEDs) will be blinking. Shifter background illumination LEDs will be turned off. A Stored DTC will be cleared after 100 ignition cycles if the failure does not reoccur.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CAN DPT CIRCUIT OPEN CIRCUIT</li><li>CAN DPT CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>CAN DPT CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>TCM CAN DPT SHORTED OR OPEN INTERNALLY</li><li>ELECTRONIC SHIFT CONTROL MODULE (ESM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Electronic Shift Module (ESM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ESM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE CONTROLLER AREA NETWORK (CAN) DEDICATED POWERTRAIN (DPT) CIRCUIT VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ESM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (D441) CAN DPT (+) circuit at the ESM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (D440) CAN DPT (-) circuit at the ESM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage between 2.4 and 2.6 volts for each circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the ESM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SHIFTER, TRANSMISSION, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK CAN DPT CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Transmission Control Module (TCM) harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D441) CAN DPT (+) circuit between the ESM harness connector and the TCM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D440) CAN DPT (-) circuit between the ESM harness connector and the TCM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms for each circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the affected CAN DPT circuit(s) for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK CAN DPT CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (D441) CAN DPT (+) circuit at the TCM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (D440) CAN DPT (-) circuit at the TCM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the either of the CAN DPT circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the affected CAN DPT circuit(s) for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK CAN DPT CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO ANOTHER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between the (D441) CAN DPT (+) circuit and all other circuits at the TCM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for continuity between the (D440) CAN DPT (-) circuit and all other circuits at the TCM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between either CAN DPT circuit and any other circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the affected CAN DPT circuit(s) for a short to another circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace the ESM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ELECTRONIC SHIFT (ESM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u145d-00 implausible data received from tcm on d-pt\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U145D-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM TCM ON D-PT</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من TCM ON D-PT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Sensor information and other calculated data that is processed by an Electronic Control Module (ECU) can be transmitted over the Controller Area Network (CAN). Some ECUs require information from other ECUs to check the validity of the information relative to that system. In some cases that information is used in the calculations relative to that ECU.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the transmitting ECU knows that the data is not valid, it will transmit a CAN message indicating that the information is not valid or not available. Often, this message is known as a Signal Not Available (SNA) message.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When a SNA message is transmitted, a Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will be set in the receiving ECU.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If a SNA message is received, this indicates that the transmitting ECU cannot transmit good data relative to the information that it was supposed to send. Typically, the transmitting ECU will also have a DTC set related to that information. Therefore, in most cases, this DTC is considered informational because the error is related to another ECU.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage message received over Controller Area Network (CAN) is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts If system voltage over CAN is not available, Electronic Shift Module (ESM) sensed voltage is used and must be between 6.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Dedicated Powertrain (DPT) Bus Off Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) set. The ESM is programmed. The Transmission Control Module (TCM) is available on the CAN bus.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The TCM has transmitted a message indicating that the expected data is not valid.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">All shift indicator Light Emitting Diodes (LEDs) will be blinking unless communication on CAN C is still valid. The DTC will be Stored once the ESM receives valid data related to the information it was expecting. A Stored DTC will be cleared after 100 ignition cycles if the failure does not reoccur.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) DTCS ARE SET</li><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODES (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Electronic Shift Module (ESM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Event Data and Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Event and Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ESM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Transmission Control Module (TCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any TCM DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair TCM DTCs. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the Transmission Control Module (TCM) connector and all related in-line connector terminals for corrosion, damage, or pushed out terminals. Pay particular attention to the power and ground circuits. If no problems are found, replace and program the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this circuit.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wiggle the wires while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check for any Service Bulletins that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">STANDARD PROCEDURE PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For a complete wiring diagram, refer to Wiring Information .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Pre-Diagnostic Troubleshooting Procedure is intended to provide the technician with a common starting point for all DTC troubleshooting procedures. The DTC troubleshooting procedures assume that the following steps have been performed and therefore are not always repeated. Failure to follow the steps in this procedure can lead to misdiagnosis.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If any repairs are performed, perform the appropriate VERIFICATION TEST.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Do not perform repairs not related to the customer complaint.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, run a Vehicle Scan Report and a ECU Configuration Report and save the files for future use.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check the vehicle repair history for any recent repairs that may be related to the customer complaint.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If possibly related to the customer complaint, verify the vehicle build configuration with the OEM Vehicle Build Configuration on TechCONNECT. Properly configure the vehicle if necessary.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If possibly related to the customer complaint, verify all Electronic Control Units (ECU)s have the same Original Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) . If a mismatch is found, this could indicate the source of the problem. Typically, this condition will cause multiple communication DTCs to set however, this is not always the case.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With a scan tool, check all ECUs for available software updates that are related to the customer complaint. Read Service Bulletins to determine if the software update is applicable to the customer complaint. Update the (ECU)s if necessary.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Use the Search function in TechCONNECT to read any related information under SERVICE ACTIONS/TIPS .</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform any Service Bulletins or other procedures that may apply.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Check for aftermarket electrical accessories . Be certain they are installed properly and do not interfere with any related power, ground, signal, or communication circuits. Be certain aftermarket wiring harnesses are routed away from vehicle wiring harness to avoid electromagnetic interference (EMI) where applicable.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A low battery State Of Charge (SOC) or a charging system that is not operating properly can cause many symptoms and DTCs to set.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>If possibly related to the customer complaint, check the vehicle charging system and battery for proper operation . Refer to the appropriate Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Check other ECUs for DTCs that could cause this DTC to set.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>If multiple DTCs are set in one ECU, and no detectable pattern is evident (i.e. the DTCs are not related to</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">just one or two components or subsystems), check the applicable ECU ground circuit(s) for proper continuity . As a general rule, diagnose the DTCs in the following order unless instructed otherwise by the specific DTC procedure:</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>ECU Configuration DTCs</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>ECU Voltage DTCs</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>ECU Internal Error DTCs</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Communication DTCs (See below)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Circuit Fault DTCs (Low voltage, High Voltage, Open Circuit, Short Circuit, Low Current, High Current, etc.,)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Performance / Rationality DTCs</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Implausible or Invalid Data</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Missing Message</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Other</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>If multiple communication DTCs are set, diagnose the DTCs in the following order unless instructed otherwise by the specific DTC procedure:</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CAN Bus Off</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CAN Bus Off Performance</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Lost Communication</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Other</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           IMPORTANT: Some Control Modules simply pass information from one Control Module to the other. In some cases, a U-code DTC may be set that implicates the &quot;pass-through&quot; module that sent the information. For example, if an Engine Coolant Temperature (ECT) Sensor DTC is set in the Powertrain Control Module (PCM), the HVAC module may set an &quot;Implausible Data from BCM&quot; DTC because the BCM is the module that normally passes that information from the PCM to the HVAC module. However, the BCM may not set any DTCs related to the faulted ECT Sensor because the BCM does not use the ECT information. In this case, the PCM ECT DTC should be diagnosed before the Implausible Data DTC. If you suspect a scenario like this, diagnose the non U-code DTC(s) before diagnosing any Implausible Data, Implausible Signal, Invalid Data, or Missing Message DTCs.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Perform the following procedure to verify proper Electronic Shift Module (ESM) operation after repairs have been performed.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Reinstall any removed components.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect any disconnected electrical connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, display the Transmission Temperature.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Start the engine and allow the Transmission fluid temperature to reach 43°C (110°F).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the brakes applied, slowly change the Shifter position to each of the available positions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>The Shift indicators should indicate the correct position for each of the available positions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, read ESM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Did any ESM DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair ESM DTCs. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Article GUID: A00910376</p></div></div></details></div></details></div>";
